diagnostic_evidence.quote:
With the change of variable $v:= (1- \exp(-\ml u(x))/\lambda$, we see that $v$ solves

\begin{equation}\label{eq:gen_transform}
     H(x, \nabla v) + \ml f(x) v= 0.
\end{equation}

Similarly, we may apply this transform to the time dependent equation
\begin{equation}
    u_t+H(x,\nabla u) = 0,
\end{equation}
where $\cH(x,p)$ is positively homogeneous of degree 1 in $p$.
